# The stage0 compiler's back end: a checked program written as one C file, to
# be linked with the runtime of refined executables, the runtime in
# SemanticScript as an object (`refined build semanticscript/runtime --kind
# runtime`), which starts the process, writes output, traps with exit code 70,
# keeps regions, and runs the host library as `refined build --kind
# executable` programs do, with no C library (D-142). The file is:
#
# - a fixed prelude: declarations of the runtime functions it calls, text as a
#   pointer and a length, the checked arithmetic, string.advancePosition, and
#   lists (a header {length, capacity, data, region, identity} and a data block
#   that starts at four items and doubles, allocated in the list's region as
#   the LLVM backend allocates them, so a region's maxBytes is reached at the
#   same call);
# - then each module in source order. Every name a module declares is written
#   `<module>_<name>` (D-114). Each record is a struct of its fields
#   (`m_<field>`), each enum a struct of an `int32_t tag` and either one
#   `int64_t payload` (the narrow layout, when every payload is an integer, a
#   Bool, or an enum without payloads) or one field per payload (`p_<variant>`),
#   the LLVM backend's layouts, so sizes agree; `rl_<Type>` for a type that
#   holds text, which copies the text into a region (as a collection does with
#   what it stores, and a return with an output owned by a region);
#   `fl_<Type>` and `uf_<Type>`, which flatten a value to the 64-bit slots
#   the host reads and read it back; `la_`, `lg_`, `lt_`, and `ls_<List>` for
#   each list's append, get, getOrTrap, and set; `mn_`, `mp_`, `mg_`, `mc_`,
#   `mr_`, `ml_`, and `mk_<Map>` for each map's members, calls of the host's
#   map (D-116); each operationType as a function pointer type; each table as
#   a static array `tb_<table>` of its rows and `tr_<table>` reading row 1 to
#   n; the module's constants as static C values `k_<module>_<name>`; and
#   each operation as `static ... o_<module>_<name>(...)`: it returns its
#   output, or, when it raises, a bool that is true on failure with the output
#   and error written through `ss_out` and `ss_err`. Its values are C locals
#   `v_<name>` (its module's constants among them), each call that can fail
#   has a flag `f_<call>`, each bounded loop a counter `n_<label>`, each
#   forEach loop a position `i_<label>`, and each label a C label `l_<label>`
#   followed by its steps. A recursive operation counts its depth in
#   `d_<module>_<name>` and traps past its maxRecursion. A target of the host
#   library is one call of the runtime's `refined_host`, its arguments and
#   result flattened to 64-bit slots as the LLVM backend flattens them, a
#   scoped target's last argument the scope text (D-38);
# - `refined_program_main`, which the runtime's entry runs (it reads the
#   command line itself), returning the entry operation's ExitCode.
#
# A jump to a bounded loop header counts the pass when it comes from inside
# the loop (from the header or a block within it) and resets the count (and a
# forEach loop's position) when it enters the loop from outside, the rule the
# LLVM backend follows, so a loop that passes its bound traps in C as it does
# under `refined run`.
#
# This module is generated from tools/emitc.dsl by tools/build.py; it is
# ordinary SemanticScript and is checked as such.

emitc is module
emitc purpose "Write a checked stage0 program as one C file"
emitc path emitc
emitc imports standard.string
emitc imports standard.buffer
emitc imports standard.list
emitc imports standard.map
emitc imports standard.math
emitc imports standard.compare
emitc imports standard.logic
emitc imports standard.test
emitc imports lexer
emitc imports syntax
emitc imports model
emitc imports subset
emitc exports emitProgram

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C spellings
CTarget is record
CTarget purpose "How a standard library target is written in C: the text before, between, and after its arguments; or, for a target of the host library, the name refined_host dispatches on, with how many 64-bit slots its arguments and result take, and for a scoped target the effect (verb and resource) whose scope text it is given last"
CTarget typeParameter none
CTarget field text String
CTarget field before String
CTarget field between String
CTarget field after String
CTarget field host Bool
CTarget field key String
CTarget field slots Int64
CTarget field results Int64
CTarget field scoped Bool
CTarget field verb String
CTarget field resource String

CType is record
CType purpose "How a built-in type is written in C"
CType typeParameter none
CType field text String
CType field cType String

cTargets is table
cTargets purpose "The C spelling of every standard library target of the subset, in the order of subset's builtinTargets"
cTargets rowType CTarget
cTargets row consoleWriteLineSpelling 1
cTargets row consoleWriteSpelling 2
