emitProgram is operation
emitProgram purpose "Check a modelled program and write it as one C file: the prelude, each module in source order (its types, constants, prototypes, and operations), and a C main that runs the entry operation"
emitProgram invariant writesC "\"Writes the prelude, then for each module typedefs and structs for its records, enums, lists, maps, and operationTypes, relocators, flatteners, list and map helpers, tables, constants, a prototype per operation, and each operation as a C function whose labels and steps follow in source order; then a C main returning the entry operation's ExitCode. Every name a module declares is written `<module>_<name>`, so modules may share names\""
emitProgram invariant countsLoopPasses "\"A jump to a bounded loop header from inside the loop counts a pass, which traps past the bound; a jump from outside resets the count, and a forEach loop's position\""
emitProgram invariant refusesOutsideSubset "\"A program outside the subset is refused at the first word concerned, as checkProgram refuses it, and a program whose entry is not an operation is refused at its module\""
